the 290 meter long stricken Cruiser the  cost of Concordia has lain here for 19  months now the attempt at removing it in  one piece is set to begin in earnest but  it's an unprecedented and risky  technical challenge and there are other  factors too if the weather conditions  permit will start the operation at 6  a.m. on Monday the plan is to use  hydraulic pumps and cables to lift the  partially submerged wreck off the island  of Giglio to an upright position that  part of the salvage operation alone  could take up to 12 hours the second  stage envisages a set of giant steel  containers being welded to the wreck  they would help to refloat the Concordia  before it is total pot but ever since  running aground the ship's hull has been  sinking lower and lower into the sea the  salvage team will only have one attempt  at stabilizing the vessel the shipping  operator estimates the cost of salvaging  the Concordia at around 600 million  euros there's no guarantee of success  the ship could break apart at any time  further threatening the environment and  permanently sinking the dreams of the  salvage team
 

